@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+---
+"emdash": minor
+"@emdash-cms/plugin-types": minor
+"@emdash-cms/plugin-cli": minor
+"@emdash-cms/cloudflare": minor
+"@emdash-cms/sandbox-workerd": minor
+---
+
+Adds `ctx.authorization.check()` for trusted and sandboxed plugins that declare `authorization:check`. Plugins can ask whether an original user may currently publish a particular content entry after delayed work completes.
+
+The host reads current account eligibility, native permissions, and content ownership for every call and returns only `{ allowed: boolean }`. The capability grants neither user-directory access nor content mutation. Existing installations must consent to the additional capability before it becomes available.
+
+The initial permissions are `content:publish_own` and `content:publish_any`, for publish and unpublish. A decision is point-in-time; callers still need native revision concurrency and publication lifecycle safeguards. It does not make a subsequent mutation atomic with authorization.
